# docs/PROGRESS.md was 1397 lines and is now an index. The full text of all
# prior sessions moved here, unedited, rather than being cut. Tracked so the
# citations from docs/performance/ resolve on a clone.
!/docs/internal/
!/docs/internal/**
# The first of the three first-hour documents: README -> quickstart -> authoring.
# Commands only, no prose, and it runs.
!/docs/quickstart.md
# The worked example the README Quickstart ingests. It is a plain ADR with no
# frontmatter and no `claims:` block, which is the thing being demonstrated, so
# it has to be a real file on a clean clone.
!/docs/adr/
!/docs/adr/**
# Registering the agent. Three clients, three config shapes, and the README points
# here for them, so the file has to survive a clone or the link 404s on a fresh
# checkout. tests/test_mcp_client_docs.py parses the JSON in it and checks every
# tool name against what the server actually advertises.
!/docs/mcp.md
# Material that was built, proved, and then deliberately withdrawn. It is part of
# the project's record: without it the next person re-derives the same findings
# and the same 42501. Not runnable from here -- it lives outside tests/ on purpose.
!/docs/withdrawn/
!/docs/withdrawn/**
!/docs/evaluation/
/docs/evaluation/*
!/docs/evaluation/m006.md
!/docs/operations.md
!/docs/m009/
!/docs/m009/**
!/docs/performance/
!/docs/performance/**
monitoring/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Markdown. Session 10.
#
# This used to be `*.md` plus a hand-maintained list of exceptions, and the list
# was the failure. Four documents -- docs/wedge-decision-note.md,
# docs/release/tag-checklist.md, docs/release/v1.0.0-readiness.md and
# docs/evaluation/m007-jev-decision-layer-spike.md -- were written, reported as
# deliverables, and never committed. docs/PROGRESS.md quoted one of them for
# three sessions. A new document was silently dropped nine times before anyone
# noticed, because nothing failed.
#
# The rule now is the opposite: **tracked by default**, with the ignored set
# written as explicit, named paths. A new .md file is committed unless somebody
# deliberately decided otherwise, which is the only direction that fails safe.
#
# scripts/check_doc_paths.py fails the build if a claim-bearing document names a
# path git does not track, and fails again if an ignored Markdown file appears
# under docs/ or eval/ with no rule saying it should be.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Explicit scratch. The ONLY Markdown this project deliberately does not ship:
# personal notes, half-written plans, and session handoffs for finished work.
# Anything a future session would need to act on belongs in docs/.
/scratch/

# The decision log is the example's input, not prose about the example. Without
# the negation the example raises SystemExit on its first line in a fresh clone.
!examples/project-log/**/*.md

# eval/results was deliberately untracked: nine frozen artifacts there are cited
# by name from tracked documents, so a clone could not resolve those citations,
# and no guard reading `git ls-files` could cover them.
#
# The owner has approved tracking them. They are measurements, and unlike the
# rest of the benchmark output they are the ones the documentation depends on --
# docs/evaluation/m006.md and m00675-reproducibility.md name all nine by path.
# With them tracked, `scripts/check_frozen.py` enforces their SHA-256, which is
# the thing a git-diff-over-ignored-files could never do.
#
# See docs/internal/progress-history.md Session 10 section 1d for the original
# reasoning.
!/eval/results/

# eval/m007/adjudication/*.md -- the M007.1 blind-review protocol.
#
# Session 10 held these back because tracking them would make
# `git diff v0.9.0..HEAD -- eval/` non-empty for the first time, and the hard
# rule that session was working under said frozen files do not change.
#
# The owner has since approved tracking them: they are methodology, not
# measurements, and without them a study that ran is undocumented. They sit
# beside data that has always been tracked (review_set.jsonl, schema.json,
# adjudication_template.jsonl, reviewer-materials-manifest.json), they were
# written for the v0.5.1 milestone, and they were invisible only because a
# blanket `*.md` swallowed them.
#
# Both are in docs/performance/frozen-manifest.json with their digests, so
# "do not modify" is now enforced rather than merely intended.

# The retrieval lab's embedding cache, kept ignored after the lab was removed:
# binary .npy blobs keyed by content hash, several megabytes, worthless on
# another machine. 596 of them were committed by accident in 7ac19e6 and are being
# purged from this branch. The entry stays so a stale local directory left by an
# earlier checkout does not show up as untracked.
.retrieval_lab_cache/
